    "exam": "GATE-2016 : 2M",
    "body": "The following function computes 𝑋^𝑌 for positive \nintegers X and Y. \n int exp (int X, int Y )  { \n int res = 1, a = X, b = Y ; \n while (b != 0){ \n          if (b % 2==0) \n             { a=a* a ; b = b / 2 ;} \n         else { res = res*a;  b = b –1 ; \n }   \n return res;     } \n Which one of the following conditions is TRUE \nbefore every iteration of the loop? \n (a) XY = ab \n (b) (res * a)Y = (res * X)b  \n (c) XY = res * ab \n (d) XY = (res * a)b  \n \nControl Flow Statements",
