    "solution": "if (b % 2 = = 0) \n { a = a*a; b= b/2; }// when b is even \n else \n { \n res = res *a;// executes when b is odd \n b = b –1;} \n Let X = 3, Y = 5 \n This code will compute = 35 \n Initially, res = 1, a = 3, b = 5 \n 1st iteration \n As b is odd,  \n res = 1*3 = 3 \n b = 5 – 1 = 4 \n After 1st iteration \n a = 3, b = 4, res = 3, X = 3, Y = 5 \n Let us check all option after \n 1st iteration (before 2nd iteration) \n (a) XY = ab \n  35 = 34(false) \n (b) (res*a)Y = (res*X)b \n         (3*3)5 = (3*3)4(false) \n (c) XY = res*ab \n            35 = 3*34(true) \n        (d)  XY = (res*a)b \n         35 = (3*3)4(false) \n Hence option C is correct option (this is option \nelimination method).",
