    "type": "MCQ",
    "exam": "GATE-2017 : 2M",
    "body": "Consider the C functions foo and bar given below: \n int foo (int val)    {                                                 \n int x=0; \n while (val > 0)   { \n          x = x + foo(val – –);   \n         } \n   return val; \n } \n int bar (int val) { \n int x = 0 ; \n while (val >0){ \n       x = x + bar(val –1) ;  \n      } \n return val; \n } \n Invocation of foo(3) and bar(3) will result in: \n (a) Return of 6 and 6 respectively. \n (b) Infinite loop and abnormal termination \nrespectively \n (c) Abnormal termination and infinite loop \nrespectively \n (d) Both terminating abnormally.",
    "subject": "C Programming",
