    "solution": "12\n 1 3 4A  = n =22 79\n\n  \n for (i = 1; i < 2; i ++) \n { \n  for (j = 1; j ≤ 2;  j++) \n  { \n   temp = A [i] [j] + C; \n   A [i] [j] = A [j] [i]; \n   A [j][i] = temp – C; \n  } \n } \n (i)  if i = 1 for j = 1 \n   temp = A [1] [1] + 100 = 103 \n   A [1] [1] = A [1] [1] \n   A [1] [1] = 103 – 100 = 3 \n   No effect on A11 \n   for j = 2 \n   temp = A [1] [2] + 100 = 104 \n   A [1] [2] = 7 \n   A [2] [1] = 104 – 100 = 4 \n \n New matrix:  A12 swapped with A21. \n\n \nArrays and Linked List \n (ii) i = 2 \n    for  j = 1 \n    Temp = A [2] [1] + 100 = 104 \n    A [2] [1] = A [1] [2] = 7 \n    A [1] [2] = 104 – 100 = 4 \n    Temp = 9 + 100 = 109 \n    Matrix = \n34\n79\n\n  \n    Again, A21 swapped with A12. \n    for j = 2 \n    temp = 9 + 100 = 109 \n     A [2] [2] = A [2] [2] \n     A [2] [2] = 109 – 100 = 9 \n    No effect. \n Finally, we get the same matrix \n• Aij is swapped with its mirror image Aji (Lower \ntriangular gular/upper triangular) \n• And when the code executes for the mirror \nimage again both elements are swapped  \n  Same matrix",
