    "day": 6,
    "answerKey": "c",
    "solution": "Code – 1  \n   for (i  = 0; i < n ; 1+ +) \n   Y [i]+ = X [0][i] \n   X [i] [i] = + I + j \n   X [0] [i] \n   for (i =0; I < n, i + +) \n  Y [i]+ = i \n Code – 2   \n   for (i = 0; i < n; i+j) \n   Y [i]+ = X [i] [0] \n   X [i] [j] = i + j \n   X [i] [0] = i \n   For (i  = 0; i < n; i ++) \n  Y [i] + = i; \n Result is same in both segment  \n  For (i= 0; i < n ; 1+j) \n  Y [i] + = X [0][i]; \n           Suppose, n = 3; \n  i = 0 X [0] [0] \n\n \nProgramming and Data Structures \n \n  i = 1 X [0] [1] \n  i = 2 X [0] [2] \n  i = 3 X [0] [3] \n  In C, by default row major order is followed  \n   elements are stored contiguously.  \n In Code – 2  \n  i = 0 X [0] [0] \n  i = 1 X [0] [0] \n  i = 2 X [2] [0] \n  i = 3 X [3] [0] \n In C, Row major order is followed  \n   elements are not stored contiguously.  \n Row major order: \n  \n00 01 02 03\n10 11 12 13\n20 21 22 23\n30 31 32 33\n0 1 2 3\n0 X  X  X  X1 X  X  X  X2\nX  X  X  X3\nX  X  X  X\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n Stored data row wise and access the data row wise.",
