    "body": "Consider a quadratic equation x2 - 13x + 36 = 0 with \ncoefficients in a base b. The solutions of this equation \nin the same base b are x = 5 and x = 6. Then b =_____.",
    "subject": "Digital Logic",
    "chapter": "Number Systems & Binary Codes",
    "day": 36,
    "answerKey": "8",
    "solution": "Given the base of quadratic equation is b. \n (1)b x2 – (13)b x + (36)b = (0)b \n x2 – (b + 3)x + 3b + 6 = 0 \n Let x = 5 \n 25 – (b + 3)5 + 3b + 6 = 0 \n 25 – 5b – 15 + 3b + 6 = 0 \n                       16 – 2b = 0 \n                                b = 8 \n Let x = 6 \n 36 – (b + 3)6 + 3b + 6 = 0 \n 36 – 6b – 18 + 3b + 6 = 0 \n                       24 – 3b = 0 \n                                b = 8 \n Hence correct answer is (8).",
