    "exam": "GATE-2008: 1M",
    "body": "Consider the following Boolean function of four \nvariables f(A, B, C, D) = Σ(2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, \n13) The function is \n (a) independent of one variable \n (b) independent of two variables \n (c) independent of three variable \n (d) dependent on all the variables",
    "subject": "Digital Logic",
    "chapter": "Boolean Algebra, Logic Gates & K-Maps",
    "day": 39,
    "answerKey": "a",
    "solution": "1. (d)  \n For n = 1, Total number of functions = 4 \n Total number of self-dual functions = 2 \n For n = 2, Total number of functions = 16 \n Total number self-dual functions = 4 \n Now, if we have ‘n’ variable with us \n Then total number of function = \nn22  \n Among then number of self-dual functions  \n= \nn–122  \n Self -Dual: \n F = FD \n F = AB \n FD = A+B \n \nDualAA⎯⎯⎯ →  \n \nDualAA⎯⎯ ⎯ →  \n Ex- \n F = AB + BC + AC \n FD = (A + B) (B + C) (A + C) \n FD= AB + BC + AC \n Hence, correct answer is option (d)",
    "id": "pyq_39_428"
