    "body": "The attributes of three arithmetic operators in some \nprogramming language are given below. \nOperator Precedence Associativity Arity \n+ High Left Binary \n– Medium  Right Binary \n* Low  Left Binary \n The value of the expression 2 – 5 + 1 – 7 * 3 in this \nlanguage is ________.",
    "subject": "Compiler Design",
    "chapter": "Syntax Analysis & Parsing (LL, LR, LALR)",
    "day": 59,
    "answerKey": "9 to 9",
    "solution": "Given,  \n + has highest prcedence and left associative. \n – has medium precedence and right associative. \n * has lowest precedence and left associative.  \n Expression = 2 – 5 + 1 – 7 * 3 \n          = 2- [5+1] – 7 * 3 \n                   = 2 – 6 – 7 * 3 \n                   = [2- [6 - 7]]*3 \n                   = [2-(-1)] * 3 \n                   = 3 * 3 \n                   = 9 \n So, 9 is the correct answer.",
    "id": "pyq_59_582"
