    "answerKey": "7",
    "solution": "Suppose, the initial value of S = x \n Now, 20P means 20 down operations(-20) and 12 \nV means 12 up operations (+12).  \n It is saying that at least one operation should \nremain blocked.  \n So, this can be written as, \n x – 20 + 12 = –1 \n x – 8 = –1 \n x = 7 \n So, the largest initial value of S for which  at least \none operation will remain blocked is 7.",
