    "body": "Three concurrent processes X, Y and Z execute three \ndifferent code segments that access and update \ncertain shared variables. Process X execute the P \noperation (i.e., wait) on semaphores a, b and c; \nprocess Y executes the P operation on semaphores b, \nc and d; process Z executes the P operation on \nsemaphores c, d and a before entering the respective \ncode segments. After completing the execution of its \ncode segments each process invokes the V operation \n(i.e., signal) on its three semaphores. All semaphores \nare binary semaphores initialized to one. Which one \nof the following represents a deadlock -free order of \ninvoking the P operations by the processes? \n (a) X: P(a)P(b)P(c) (b) X: P(b)P(a)P(c) \n   Y: P(b)P(c)P(d)   Y: P(b)P(c)P(d) \n   Z: P(c)P(d)P(a)   Z: P(a)P(c)P(d) \n   \n  (c) X: P(b)P(a)P(c) (d) X: P(a)P(b)P(c) \n   Y: P(c)P(b)P(d)   Y: P(c)P(b)P(d) \n   Z: P(a)P(c)P(d)   Z: P(a)P(c)P(d) \n  \n \nProcess Synchronization",
