    "num": 21,
    "type": "MCQ",
    "exam": "GATE-2022-CS: 1M",
    "body": "Consider the following threads, T 1, T 2, and T 3 \nexecuting on a single processor, synchronized using \nthree binary semaphore variables, S1, S2, and S3, \noperated upon using standard wait() and signal(). \nThe threads can be context switched in any order and \nat any time.  \nT1 T2 T3 \nwhile (true) { \n    wait (S3); \n    print(“C”); \n    signal (S 2); \n} \nwhile (true) { \n    wait (S1); \n    print(“B”); \n    signal (S 3); \n} \nwhile (true) \n   {wait (S2); \n    print(“A”); \n    signal (S 1); \n} \nWhich initialization of the semaphores would print \nthe sequence BCABCABCA…..? \n (a) S1 = 1; S2 = 1; S3 = 1 \n(b) S1 = 1; S2 = 1; S3 = 0 \n(c) S1 = 1; S2 = 0; S3 = 0 \n (d) S1 = 0; S2 = 1; S3 = 1 \n \nClassical IPC Problems",
