    "exam": "GATE-2008 : 2M",
    "body": "Which of the following is NOT true of deadlock \nprevention and deadlock avoidance schemes? \n (a) In deadlock prevention, the request for resources \nis always granted if the resulting state is safe \n (b) In deadlock avoidance, the request for resources \nis always granted if the resulting state is safe \n (c) Deadlock avoidance is less restrictive than \ndeadlock prevention \n (d) Deadlock avoidance requires knowledge of \nresource requirements a priori. \n \n Resource Allocation Graph",
    "subject": "Operating Systems",
