    "answerKey": "a",
    "solution": "Cardinality of E1 > Cardinality of E2  \n \n (a) Correct. Every entity of E 1 is associated with \nexactly one entity in E2. \n  ( its total participation and many to one from E1 \nto E2). \n (b) Incorrect. Because mention some entity in E 1 \nbut here total participati on and mention more \nthan one entity in E2 but here many to one (of E2 \nside). \n (c) Incorrect. Because there is a many to one from  \nE1 to E2, not from E2 to E1. \n (d) Incorrect. Because there is a many to one from  \nE1 to E2.",
