    "exam": "GATE-2013 : 2M",
    "body": "Relation R has eight attributes ABCDEFGH. \n Fields of R contain only atomic values. \n F = {CH → G, A → BC, B → CFH, E → A, F → EG} \nis a set of functional \n dependencies (FDs) so that F+ is exactly the set of FDs \nthat hold for R. \n How many candidate keys does the relation R have? \n (a) 3  (b) 4 \n (c) 5  (d) 6 \n \nMembership Set and Equality between FD Sets",
